    "result_text": "Tests pass and the build is green. Both findings are addressed:\n\n**Finding 1 \u2014 `fiscalYearYY` duplication (agreed, fixed).** Added `RegistrationDateNormalizer.fiscalYearYY(LocalDate)` alongside the existing `fiscalYear(date)`. Both callers now delegate to it:\n- `OwnerMapper.fiscalYear(owner)` calls `RegistrationDateNormalizer.fiscalYearYY(...)` (the private copy is gone).\n- `ClinicServiceImpl.deriveMemberId` keeps its null\u2192`LocalDate.now()` guard at the call site, then delegates the formatting. A future format change now lives in one place.\n\n**Finding 2 \u2014 region vocabulary duplication (agreed, fixed).** Extracted `rest.validation.Regions` as the single source of the region set + postcode ranges, exposing `REGION_POSTCODES`, `UNKNOWN`, `known()`, and `forPostcode(...)`:\n- `ClinicServiceImpl` (the generator) now calls `Regions.forPostcode(...)` \u2014 its private `REGION_POSTCODES`, `UNKNOWN_REGION`, `regionForPostcode`, and the now-unused `java.util.Map` import were removed.\n- `OwnerMapper.locality` (the parser) prefix-matches against `Regions.known()` and returns `Regions.UNKNOWN`, so adding a region in one place keeps generator and parser in sync. This also removed the awkward `\"UNKNOWN\"` sitting inside the iterated `REGIONS` list \u2014 `UNKNOWN` is now purely the fallback return.\n\nI also folded `PostcodeValidator`'s identical `REGION_POSTCODES` copy into the shared `Regions.REGION_POSTCODES`, so the extraction consolidates rather than adding a third copy. Its `CITY_REGION` table (a distinct city\u2192region concern) stays local.\n\nAcceptance behaviour is unchanged: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
