    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe rename and field-unification are done consistently across model, mapper, controller, audit event, and all four schema.sql dialects, and moving the Luhn digit into ID generation (`luhnCheckDigit` in `ClinicServiceImpl`, replacing the mapper's removed `checkDigit`) is a sensible relocation. Two duplication issues remain:\n\n**1. `fiscalYearYY` is now duplicated across two classes.**\n- `OwnerMapper.fiscalYearYY` (OwnerMapper.java:125-127): `String.format(\"%02d\", RegistrationDateNormalizer.fiscalYear(date) % 100)`\n- `ClinicServiceImpl.fiscalYearYY` (ClinicServiceImpl.java:511-514): the same computation, with an added null\u2192`LocalDate.now()` fallback.\n\nThese are the same \"two-digit fiscal year\" formatting rule copied into a mapper and a service. The natural home is `RegistrationDateNormalizer`, which already owns `fiscalYear(date)` \u2014 add a `fiscalYearYY(date)` (or `%100`/`%02d`) helper there and have both callers delegate. As written, a future change to the fiscal-year format must be made in two places that don't reference each other.\n\n**2. The region vocabulary is duplicated between the mapper and the service.**\n- `OwnerMapper.REGIONS = List.of(\"NSW\", \"VIC\", \"QLD\", \"UNKNOWN\")` (OwnerMapper.java:144), used by `locality()` to prefix-match a region out of the delimiter-less `memberId`.\n- `ClinicServiceImpl.REGION_POSTCODES` keys (`NSW`/`VIC`/`QLD`) plus `UNKNOWN_REGION` (ClinicServiceImpl.java:483-487) are what actually *generate* the region prefix.\n\nThe generator (service) and the parser (mapper) now each hard-code the region set independently. Adding a region requires editing both, and there is no compile-time link keeping them in sync \u2014 a maintainer adding \"TAS\" to `REGION_POSTCODES` would silently get `locality() == \"UNKNOWN\"` for those members. Previously `locality()` was self-describing (split on the `-` delimiter) and needed no region knowledge; the format change forced prefix-matching, so the region vocabulary should be sourced from one shared place rather than re-declared in the mapper. (Note `\"UNKNOWN\"` sitting inside `REGIONS` is also awkward, since it's simultaneously the fallback return value.)\n\nBoth are straightforward to address by extracting the shared helpers/constants; neither blocks the intent of the change.",
